---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'

const title = "Base44 not working: a calm triage order"
const description = "Status first, then publish, blank screen, domain, and schema when Base44 is not working."
const datePublished = "2026-09-01"
const url = 'https://base44expert.com/blog/base44-not-working'

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BlogPosting',
    headline: title,
    description,
    datePublished,
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Base44 Expert' },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Base44 Expert', url: 'https://base44expert.com' },
    mainEntityOfPage: url,
    url,
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://base44expert.com/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: 'https://base44expert.com/blog' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: title, item: url },
    ],
  },
]
---

<Layout title={`${title} — Base44 Expert`} description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <main id="main">
    <article class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <p class="label-eyebrow mb-2">
          <a href="/blog" class="underline underline-offset-2">Blog</a>
          <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
          <time datetime={datePublished}>{datePublished}</time>
        </p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl text-ink mb-8 text-balance">{title}</h1>
        <div class="prose-studio text-stone leading-relaxed space-y-4">
          <p>When someone says “Base44 not working,” they usually mean one concrete stuck moment: publish failed, live output did not change, blank screen after an edit, domain pending, or data missing.</p>
          <p>Start at <a href="https://status.base44.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">status.base44.com</a>. If Hosting or Builder is degraded, do not burn credits rewriting the app.</p>
          <p>Next, separate publish problems from domain problems from schema problems. Our page on <a href="/base44-not-working">Base44 not working</a> lists that order. Official notes live in <a href="https://docs.base44.com/Community-and-support/Troubleshooting" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">docs troubleshooting</a>.</p>
          <p>If you are past status and still stuck, <a href="/start">start a diagnostic</a> with the error text and app URL.</p>

        </div>
        <p class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-line">
          <a href="/start" class="btn-primary">Start a diagnostic</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
